# ULX Lab essentials

## Boundaries

- Implement **only** in this `ulx-lab` repo.
- **Never** edit Eventz or `ulx-components` source (`../ulx-components/src`).
- Do not add library demos under `ulx-components`. This app consumes ULX; it does not author the library.

## Screens

- Presentational UI lives in `app/components/screens/*.gjs`.
- Shared editor chrome lives in `app/components/commons/` (`home-page-template`, `event-page-template`, home/event top and left bars). When adding a page, wrap it in the matching page template.
- Static fixtures live in `app/mocks/*.js`.
- Thin route + template glue supplies mocks and `@onSave` / `@onCancel` (or similar args).
- Register every new screen in `app/data/screens.js` and `app/router.js`.
- Public API is args only. No Ember Data, no real APIs, no Eventz models or services.
- Use Ember 6.8 Glimmer `.gjs`: `@tracked`, `@action`, barrel imports (`import { UlxButton } from 'ulx-components'`).
- User-facing copy is plain English literals. Eventz i18n happens at copy time.

## Tune, do not regenerate

- After a screen exists, property changes (size, width, variant, label) are **surgical arg edits**, not a new screen.
- Lift tunable ULX args onto the presentational component (`@size`, `@width`, …) with a `SCREEN_DEFAULTS` block.
- Add lab-only controls in `app/data/controls/` and register them in `app/data/screen-settings.js`. The application top bar **Settings** control opens a `UlxSlidePane` with `LabArgControls` (`@screenId` required so changes persist). Demo routes stay demos — do not put the inspector on the screen template or a settings route.
- For UlxModal `@size`, use `optionsFrom: 'dialog.sizes'` (tokens from `uls_v2` `dialog.less`, generated at build into `app/data/uls-tokens/dialog.js`). Do not hardcode XS–XL.
- Adjusting a control **writes the presentational `.gjs` defaults** via `/__lab/persist-args` (`ember serve` only). Do not regenerate the screen.
- Register persistable screens in `server/index.js` `LAB_SCREENS`.

## Components and styling

- Compose existing `Ulx*` components. Do not invent wrappers that re-skin ULX internals.
- CSS classes: only ULS v2 / ULX utilities. No new CSS files, no inline styles, no ad-hoc class names.
- Named blocks: lowercase; if any named block exists, put body in `<:default>`. Prefer `@argument` over a named block when the API already covers the case.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, `...attributes` where needed, `@dataQa` on interactive ULX controls.
- Theme is **editor** (`ulx-editor.less`). Do not switch to community/onair unless asked.

## Skills

- Choosing a control → `ulx-component-discovery`
- Application layout/styling → `ulx-consumer-ui`
- Forms → `ulx-form-patterns`
- Overlays, menus, feedback → `ulx-ui-patterns`
- Tables, lists, cards → `ulx-data-display-patterns`
- Copying into Eventz → `ulx-lab-handoff`
